  "rationale": "The agent produced the required CSV schema and its execution log supports that it ran a CLR-based, custom elastic-net quantile-regression workflow. However, it did not implement the requested/reference determination of taxa present at tau=0.9 and absent at tau=0.5. The reference uses a 1e-6 nonzero criterion and takes the set difference, with alpha=0.1 and no feature standardization. In contrast, the agent used different preprocessing and hyperparameters (multiplicative zero replacement, StandardScaler, alpha=0.01); its logged fits did not converge at any quantile; and it defined “not average” using arbitrary 75th/25th percentile coefficient cutoffs even though 497/500 median-model coefficients were nonzero. This materially changes the reported set and cannot be regarded as a reasonable implementation difference. The resulting 7 taxa conflict markedly with the 106 reference taxa, including an opposite sign for shared Taxon_471.",
