    "reason": "The agent produced the required CSV schema and its execution log supports that it ran a CLR-based, custom elastic-net quantile-regression workflow. However, it did not implement the requested/reference determination of taxa present at tau=0.9 and absent at tau=0.5. The reference uses a 1e-6 nonzero criterion and takes the set difference, with alpha=0.1 and no feature standardization. In contrast, the agent used different preprocessing and hyperparameters (multiplicative zero replacement, StandardScaler, alpha=0.01); its logged fits did not converge at any quantile; and it defined “not average” using arbitrary 75th/25th percentile coefficient cutoffs even though 497/500 median-model coefficients were nonzero. This materially changes the reported set and cannot be regarded as a reasonable implementation difference. The resulting 7 taxa conflict markedly with the 106 reference taxa, including an opposite sign for shared Taxon_471.",
    "reference_method": "CLR adds a 1e-6 pseudocount, then fits an IRLS ElasticNet model without feature standardization at tau 0.1, 0.5, and 0.9 using alpha=0.1 and l1_ratio=0.5. A taxon is associated at a quantile when |coefficient| > 1e-6; reported taxa are the tau=0.9 nonzero set minus the tau=0.5 nonzero set.",
    "agent_method": "The executed custom proximal-gradient workflow replaces zeros multiplicatively, CLR-transforms and standardizes features, then fits elastic-net pinball-loss models at alpha=0.01 and l1_ratio=0.5. The logs state all fits reached the 10,000-iteration maximum without meeting tolerance. The final report selects taxa with |tau=0.9 coefficient| above its 75th percentile and |tau=0.5 coefficient| below its 25th percentile, rather than taxa absent from the tau=0.5 model.",
